Subject: Input Data size of HBase Table in RHIPE
Message-ID: <BJ_oFp0UoYs.Yy2fkyWjtYoJ@rhipe.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rhipe/c/BJ_oFp0UoYs/m/Yy2fkyWjtYoJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

I am trying  to fetch data from HBase, using custom TableInputFormat, I am sending <Key,Value> to MapReduce job.
I am trying to run MapReduce via RHIPE. I am facing problem to know exact size of input file.
HDFS_BYTES_READ just give size of .META size, it doesn't give whole table size.  How can I know Input size of HBASE Table in RHIPE?

Regards
Bikash

From u5b0c9158bfa781ba at groups.google.com  Mon Jun  3 17:13:05 2013
From: u5b0c9158bfa781ba at groups.google.com (Saptarshi Guha)
Date: Mon, 03 Jun 2013 17:13:05 +0000
Subject: Re: [rhipe] Input Data size of HBase Table in RHIPE
Message-ID: <BJ_oFp0UoYs.MNGcceUV_kcJ@rhipe.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <BJ_oFp0UoYs.Yy2fkyWjtYoJ@rhipe.groups.google.com>
References: <BJ_oFp0UoYs.Yy2fkyWjtYoJ@rhipe.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rhipe/c/BJ_oFp0UoYs/m/MNGcceUV_kcJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In your input format, create a counter of the bytes you've read (i.e. size of the key and value)
and add them to get an approximation of the of the total bytes read from HBASE.

And if you send raw bytes to RHIPE, then you can do the same via rhcounter on the RHIPE side.
But it's a few lines in java, so you might as well save time and do it java(inputformat side)

Cheers
Saptarshi

