Quick question, is this your download

http://ml.stat.purdue.edu/rhipebin/Rhipe_0.73.1.tar.gz

If so, it should work... I am using CDH 4.2 along with Cloudera manager and RHIPE works just fine.

Try and we shall help. Your notes will improve the documentation which is ... nil.

Regards
Saptarshi

What i do is (in R)
Sys.setenv(
             "JAVA_HOME"="/usr/lib/jvm/java-sun/"
             ,"HADOOP"          =sprintf("/usr/lib/hadoop")
             ,"HADOOP_HOME"    = "empty"
             ,"HADOOP_LIBS"    = paste("/usr/local/hadoopCDH4/hadoop-2.0.0-mr1-cdh4.2.1/",
                "/usr/local/hadoopCDH4/hadoop-2.0.0-cdh4.2.1/share/hadoop/hdfs/",
                "/usr/local/hadoopCDH4/hadoop-2.0.0-cdh4.2.1/share/hadoop/common/",
                "/usr/local/hadoopCDH4/hadoop-2.0.0-cdh4.2.1/share/hadoop/httpfs/",
                "/usr/local/hadoopCDH4/hadoop-2.0.0-cdh4.2.1/share/hadoop/tools/",sep=":")
             ,"HADOOP_CONF_DIR"  = "/etc/mozilla.cluster.conf/conf.peach/hadoop"
             ,"HBASE_HOME"="/usr/local/hadoopCDH4/hbase-0.94.2-cdh4.2.1" ##
             ,"HBASE_CONF_DIR"="/etc/mozilla.cluster.conf/conf.peach/hbase")

and then

Sys.setenv("RHIPE_DEBUG_LEVEL"=2L)
## #####################################
## RHIPE will not work without this
## #####################################
library(Rhipe)

if it works, you should see

Rhipe: Using RhipeCDH4.jar
Initializing Rhipe v0.73

